    "passage": "Robust growth is also forecast in the states now applying to join the EU, adding further to transport flows, road freight most of all. By 1996 several were already exporting almost three times their 1990 volumes, while their imports had climbed beyond six times the 1990 figure. Many applicant states inherited networks built around the railways, yet since the early 1990s the split between modes has swung heavily towards the road. Road haulage grew by 22.6 per cent between 1990 and 1996, whereas rail freight fell by 39.8 per cent, though rail there still runs, on average, well above the levels seen in current member states.",
