    "passage": "Professor Reinhardt Voss examined the work of Ellis Hargrove, whose plans determined the overall  of hospital buildings, allowing air to move through them freely. Using digital models, Voss demonstrated that the  carried in the breath of patients ill with  would not have reached others on the ward. He also established that the air in the  of these hospitals was replaced as often as it is in a modern surgical theatre, and that housing more patients together in  areas could reduce energy use sharply.\n\nA key force behind better ventilation in that era was pressure from ordinary  seeking protection from harmful air, which was known at the time as . Such air had been blamed for spreading disease over many centuries, including the outbreaks that struck Marseille and  around the middle of the 1800s.",
