    "title": "Is it time to halt the rising tide of plastic packaging",
    "total_questions": 3,
    "passage": "Áp dụng DOL’s Linearthinking \n\n🥰Simplify + Read connection\n\n1.  One store   commissioned = funded   a study to find precise data on which had less environmental impact: selling apples loose or ready-wrapped   \n\n 2.  in fact   apples in fours on a tray covered by plastic film   needed 27 per cent less packaging in transportation than those sold loose  . \n\n3.  Sieve Kelsey   finds the debate frustrating.  \n\n4.   the hunger to do something quickly   is diverting effort away from more complicated questions   \n\n5.  Rather than further reducing the weight of a plastic bottle ,  more thought    should be given to how packaging can be recycled.  \n\n6.  their greatest packaging reduction   came when the company switched to reusable plastic crates  \n\n7.  Plastic packaging   is important ,  and it   might provide a way of thinking about broader questions of sustainability.  \n\n8. To target plastic on its own   is to evade the complexity of the issues.  \n\n9.  There   seems to be a universal eagerness to condemn plastic.  \n\n 10.  Is this   due to an inability to make the general changes in society ?\n\n11.  Plastic as a lightweight food wrapper   is now built in as the logical thing  \n\n12.  Does that    make it an environmentally good system of packaging  ? \n\n 13.  It   only makes sense    if   you   have a structure now  \n\n14.  An environmentally driven packaging system   would look completely different  \n\n 15.  The amount of packaging used today    is a reflection of modern life.  \n\n😎 Hiểu ý chính\n\n(1) a study about environmental impact \n\n(2) findings or results of the study \n\n(3) the debate - frustrating (disagreed) \n\n(4) the hunger to do something quickly -> not solve more complicated questions \n\n(5) how packaging can be recycled \n\n(6) reusable plastic crates \n\n(7) broader questions of sustainability \n\n(8) evade the complexity of the issues \n\n(9) + (10) inability to change -> condemn plastic\n\n(11) plastic: logical thing \n\n(12) environmental good system of packaging\n\n(13) for today's structure -> it is so \n\n(13) different structure -> it is not \n\n(14) amount of packaging - reflect modern life \n\n=> Main idea: focus on plastic -> not solve the more important issues \n\n(1) + (2) Study về plastic và kết quả\n(4) The debate is driving attention away (= diverting effort away) from more complicated questions\n(5) - (15) Làm rõ “more complicated questions\" là những vấn để nào\n\n=> Main idea: Có thể thấy, đoạn này chủ yếu nói về việc tranh cãi về plastic nhưng lại không chú ý quan tâm những vấn đề lớn hơn\n\n😍 So sánh với danh sách tiêu đề:\n\nSo với list of heading: vii.  Avoiding the real challenges\n\nVì: những vấn đề lớn tức là những khó khăn thực sự, nhưng chúng bị avoid \n\nChọn heading:  vii.  Avoiding the real challenges",
