    "title": "Corporate Social Responsibility",
    "total_questions": 13,
    "passage": "1   At the heart of strategy is  a unique value proposition  :  a set of needs a company meet for its customers .\n\n2  The most strategic CSR occurs   when a company adds a social dimension to its value proposition   \n\n3  Consider Whole Foods Market,   whose value proposition is to sell natural, and healthy food to customers who are passionate about the environment .\n\n4  The company’s sourcing   emphasises purchases from local farmers.  \n\n5   Buyers    screen out foods containing ingredients that the company considers unhealthy or environmentally damaging    .\n\n6  The same standards   apply to products made internally  .\n\n7  Whole Foods’ commitment to natural and environmentally friendly operating practices   extends beyond sourcing .\n\n8  Stores    are constructed using a minimum of virgin raw materials .\n\n9  the company    purchased renewable wind energy credits   \n\n10  Spoiled produce and biodegradable waste   are trucked to regional centers for composting .\n\n11  Whole Foods’ vehicles   are being converted to run on biofuels.  \n\n12  Even the cleaning products    are environmentally friendly .\n\n13  through its philanthropy ,   the company   has created the Animal Compassion Foundation    to develop more natural ways of raising farm animals  .\n\n14 In short,   nearly every aspect of the company’s value chain    reinforces the social dimensions of its value proposition  \n\nĐọc connection:\n\nCâu 1 + 2 chỉ ra chiến lược có 1 unique value proposition - kết hợp các yếu tố vì xã hội/ vì khách hàng vào hoạt động của công ty\n\nCâu 3 lấy ví dụ về unique value proposition của Whole Foods Market - bán đồ natural và healthy cho người quan tâm tới môi trường\n\nCâu 4-> 13: đề cập tới một loạt các khía cạnh của Whole Food Market được áp dụng tiêu chuẩn natural và healthy \n\nCâu 14 chốt lại việc áp dụng tiêu chuẩn chung vì khách hàng/xã hội (value proposition/CSR) vào tất cả các khía cạnh công ty là tốt",
